From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:52:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 31/44] minimize: size window items to their title

On a top or bottom panel each item is only as wide as its icon and the
wider of its two rows need, between item_min_width and item_width. Widths
move in 20 px steps and shrink only with a whole step to spare, so a
spinner or a small title change does not move the items. When they do not
fit, the widest shrink first, then the rest overflow as before.

Titles are measured in update() only when a window's rows change.
fit_to_title = false in the sizes file keeps every item item_width wide;
fixed_width_apps lists apps that always are.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

